    <sys:String x:Key="langCliUsage" xml:space="preserve">AudioDirigent — keeps the audio output on a device that actually works.

  (no arguments)        open the window, keep running in the tray
  --tray                start in the tray without a window (used by autostart)
  --once                apply the rule once and exit
  --list                list the output devices and the current default
  --test                self-check: switching really works
  --devices             HID interfaces and the probe's answer, if one is set up
  --recover             bring vanished devices back: reinstall them and, if
                        needed, restart the audio service
  --autostart [on|off]  autostart task state, create it, remove it</sys:String>

